cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or its results, please cite the paper."
title: "autotokamak: a closed-loop benchmark for scientific machine-learning agents"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark in which a coding agent must generate its own training data from
  an expensive Grad-Shafranov plasma-equilibrium solver under a fixed budget,
  then ship a predictor scored independently on a frozen set it never sees.
  Includes a verification layer separating delivery, physical validity and
  self-report honesty, and a deterministic analysis of the method chain each
  agent built.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hindyros/autokamak"
keywords:
  - agent benchmarks
  - large language models
  - surrogate modelling
  - active learning
  - plasma equilibrium
  - scientific machine learning
